<title>FRANCE: TENNIS-STATISTICS OF HINGIS V SELES.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-STATISTICS OF HINGIS V SELES.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics of Thursday's French Open women's singles semifinal between number one seed Martina Hingis of Switzerland and third seed Monica Seles of the United States (world ranking in brackets):</p>
<p>Hingis won 6-7 (2-7) 7-5 6-4</p>
<p>Time: two hours 17 minutes</p>
<p>					HINGIS (1)	 SELES (3)</p>
<p>    Aces				2		    3</p>
<p>    Double faults		   4		    6</p>
<p>    Percentage first serves    59		   62</p>
<p>    Forehand winners	     14		   18</p>
<p>    Backhand winners	     10		    7</p>
<p>    Unforced errors		50		   71</p>
<p>    Break points		   19		   11</p>
<p>    Breaks of serve		 7		    5</p>
</text>
